Using co-interior angles at $P$ (the angle between north and $PH$ is $40^\circ$ and the bearing of $P$ from $H$ is $320^\circ$, giving $140^\circ$ at $P$):

$$\angle HPB=250^\circ-140^\circ=110^\circ$$

\exfigure{402_q16_s1}

Using the cosine rule:

$$\begin{aligned}BH^2&=5^2+4^2-2\times5\times4\cos110^\circ\\ BH^2&=41-40\cos110^\circ\\ BH&=\sqrt{41-40\cos110^\circ}\approx7.39\text{ km}\end{aligned}$$

\exfigure{402_q16_s3}

$$\dfrac{\sin\angle HBP}{4}=\dfrac{\sin110^\circ}{7.39}\ \Rightarrow\ \angle HBP=\sin^{-1}\left(\dfrac{4\sin110^\circ}{7.39}\right)\approx31^\circ$$

Bearing of $H$ from $B=70^\circ+31^\circ=101^\circ\text{T}$.

